Cloud cost governance establishes policies and operational processes that help organisations control expenditure while supporting business growth.

A typical governance framework includes:

* Budget definition
* Cost allocation
* Resource tagging
* Spending alerts
* Regular optimisation reviews
* Executive reporting

For example, each department may receive a monthly spending report based on tagged Azure resources, allowing managers to monitor usage and identify opportunities for optimisation.

A real-life use case is enterprises managing multiple Azure subscriptions while ensuring every business unit remains accountable for its cloud spending.

Effective cost governance promotes financial transparency and responsible cloud consumption.
